{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: implementation-note and evidence-path gate warning, head c435fc25ece051db42d42efc7065c2df4d48d0ae, tree fa51a49c6d04ea27d80e15e8880e2fffffeb3af5, branch builder/notes-evidence-warning-20261025. Five commits on Main 75b2233c, including one merge of 75b2233c. Seven paths, all seven named by the artifacts. Review request bd70fbbe, checker promise fa597895, request 28b878ed (builder promise 39d67a91).\n\nRead order: the primary note at the head in full; request 28b878ed; the diff of scripts/check-notes.mjs, scripts/check-notes.test.mjs, scripts/gate.sh, scripts/test.mjs and docs/testing.md; the manifest; then the gate and owning-run records in the evidence directory.\n\nBase. The head sits on 75b2233c, not on Main d1c3622f. Between those two commits only notes/reports/2026-10-25-sprint-report.md changed, which this head does not touch. git merge-tree merges the head onto d1c3622f with no conflict (tree 091059bd).\n\nHead and gate. The gate ran at checkpoint 4ec02207 (tree 402f279f). The head differs from it only in the primary note and the new manifest, so the documents-only follow-up rule applies and no second gate is owed. The owning run tested a2c026a7. Between a2c026a7 and 4ec02207 the script and its test are unchanged; the other changes are the merge of Main and the gate.sh step.\n\nAcceptance, every part met:\n1. The script warns on each case and never fails the gate. check-notes.mjs compares the committed base and head trees under notes/implementation/. It warns on each added, changed or type-changed file over 40,960 bytes, and on each added evidence path that does not end in .manifest.json. Findings exit 0. A missing base, a base that is not an ancestor, Git errors and decoding errors exit 2. In gate.sh the step uses the gate's own base (git merge-base HEAD origin/main), the same base the commit-message step uses. It runs after doc-links and prints its log when it exits 0. An exit 2 stops the later steps, as any failed step does.\n2. The Node test passes. The three cases cover the strict 40,960-byte bound (40,960 bytes is quiet, 40,961 warns, and the count is UTF-8 bytes), committed bytes despite a later working-tree edit, a new evidence name with a line break, a manifest, a changed legacy evidence file, a clean range with oversized historical files, and a missing base. scripts/test.mjs adds the file once to the Node stage. In my run from a scratch copy at the head, all three cases passed in 0.98 s.\n3. The gate passes at the reviewed checkpoint. gate-v1/result.json has exitCode 0, with expectedHead 4ec02207 and expectedTree 402f279f. In gate.stdout.log the head line shows changed files 0, install is skipped against the lockfile, and every step exits 0, including \"notes exit 0\" followed by \"notes: 0 warnings\". Node shows 56 passed (53 before, plus these 3), Counting 55, plain 2,816 passed and 1 skipped (2,817), and native 771 passed and 2 skipped (773). gate.stderr.log is empty. Rerunning test-summary.mjs on gate-v1/test-evidence shows all four stages' terminal evidence complete, and 0 contradictory records.\n4. The head carries its note and manifest under the rule (PD-2 check below).\n\nMy witness on real history, from a scratch copy of the script at the head and with the shared checkout read only:\n- 75b2233c..c435fc25 prints \"notes: 0 warnings\" and exits 0.\n- dc1be582^..dc1be582 is an older head that committed raw evidence before the rule. It prints 44 warnings, 39 of them for evidence paths that are not manifests and 5 for files over the limit, and it exits 0.\n- d1c3622f..c435fc25, where the base is not an ancestor, exits 2. The gate never passes such a base, because it uses the merge base.\n\nPD-2 manifest check. The manifest notes/implementation/evidence/2026-10-25-implementation-note-warnings.manifest.json has sha256 27abf17982d16e84be9eb1eacb9ee303001f4a82f5019b3bf07261764ed394ff, the value in the request. It records the qualification, the directory ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-25-notes-evidence-warning, checkpoint 4ec02207 / 402f279f, fileCount 63, retention, and the withheld private vectors. All 63 files are present, with matching bytes and sha256. There are no unlisted files, and no file or directory has a write bit. All 62 SHA256SUMS lines verify. The primaryNote digest 69f25d53… equals the note at the head (9,821 bytes, under the 40 KB limit). Each of the nine output digests in the note's table names a file in the manifest: owning-v1/result.json, owning-v2/stdout.log, the two dependency-copy outer-time logs, the curated filesystem audit, the setup and capture outer-time logs, gate-v1/test-evidence/node.jsonl and gate-v1/gate.stdout.log. The note keeps the two failed dependency-copy owners and the failed first owning preflight as failures. It does not count the 14 missing native ready callbacks or the 33 missing result callbacks as passes.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The check is one small read-only script with one gate hook that reuses the gate's base. It adds no new stage and no change to any test case, assertion or deadline. It compares the two trees, not each commit. A path that is added and then removed inside the range therefore gives no warning. That fits the rule, which is about what lands.\n\nSecurity: no new authority. The script runs Git with argument arrays and no shell. It uses --literal-pathspecs, and --end-of-options on rev-parse. It reads object sizes and paths only, never note contents or the working tree, and it writes nothing. Paths are printed JSON-quoted, so a filename cannot inject an extra line into the log. The test fixtures disable hooks and signing in private temporary repositories and remove them in finally. No production code, Worker, seal or deploy file changes, and no deployment is needed.\n\nSimplification: good, with two nonblocking notes.\n- A filename that is not valid UTF-8 under notes/implementation/ fails the step with exit 2, and so fails the gate. The docs name decoding errors as failures, so this is by design. If such a name ever appears, a warning would fit the advisory intent better.\n- About half of the note's evidence section is about preparing private dependency copies (owner failures, APFS link counts, filesystem audits). None of that bears on the behaviour of a 55-line script. For a head of this size, a shorter account would do: the owning run, the gate, and one line saying that setup failures are kept in the evidence directory.\n\nCommit subjects are 53 characters or fewer, and git diff --check is clean over the branch.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head c435fc25 / tree fa51a49c. The builder lands. No deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d20ca19e8409a867d1260cece378689d56b141da","binding":"assigned","head":"c435fc25ece051db42d42efc7065c2df4d48d0ae","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fa597895e2f21db31da0ecaab3899fe6087c30aa\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:39d67a9169df0cdf836acc6dcbf4930ed2461b45\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:19741d806d95eb26b204950e8ff7c6a943647b42","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}